<main class="mw-cover">
    <div class="mw-cover-page pg1">
        <div class="mw-cover-content pg1">
            <div class="mw-cover-addressee">
                <h2><span>COVER LETTER</span></h2>
                <article>
                    <time><%= new Date().toDateString() %></time>
                    <p>
                        To, <br />
                        Hiring Manager
                    </p>
                    <address>
                        Nextdoor <br/>
                        San Fransisco, CA
                    </address>
                </article>
            </div>
            <div class="mw-cover-letter">
                <h2>SENIOR SOFTWARE ENGINEER (FRONTEND) </h2>
                <article>
                    <p>To whom this may reach,</p>

                    <p>I am excited to submit my application for the role of Senior Software Engineer (Frontend) at Nextdoor. In this next step of my career I am looking for a role where I can leverage 12 years of front-end-leaning experience to lead a growing company’s efforts to scale and deliver amazing user experiences. In particular I am looking for a company that values good user experience and the attention to detail the front-end deserves.</p>
                    <p>I consider myself a user advocate, and am passionate about building good looking user interfaces which seek to enable people. In my last role, one of my biggest responsibilities was to ensure business goals and UX vision translated into a consistent product: I had numerous opportunities to advocate for the user and align expectations between product and UX. Additionally, while I’m no designer, I have an attention to detail and eye for aesthetics which makes it easy for me to work with UX designers to achieve the best look, feel, and behavior of products.</p>
                    <p>When reviewing the job description, I noticed a common theme with the expectations--line by line these were responsibilities I've held, enjoyed, and desire in a new role. My career path has given me a deep skillset in front-end development, but also a broad base of knowledge up and down the stack. I’ve spent a majority of my career owning the full lifecycle of delivery of products, and a number of opportunities to lead teams’ front-end development. This included architecting and leading the development of the company’s administrative interface which evolved into a micro-frontend platform as more teams contributed.</p>

                    <p>I am looking forward to connecting on this position and learning more about Nextdoor and this opportunity.</p>


                    <p>
                        Sincerely, <br/>
                        Matt Whitaker
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mw-cover-sidebar pg1">
            <header class="mw-cover-alt-header">
                <h1>Matt<br/>Whitaker</h1>
                <h2>SENIOR FRONT-END</h2>
            </header>
            <section class="mw-cover-contact">
                <%- await include("/template/component/contact.ejs") %>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>